*20
/THIS PROGRAM IS A DATA ACQUISITION TOOL
/TWO SENSE SWITCHES ARE USED, SN0 IS DE-
/PRESSED AFTER THE TAPE ON UNIT ONE IS 
/CHANGED TO INDICATE COMPLETION.  SN5
/IS DEPRESSED IF AVERAGES AND SPIKE HISTOGRAMS
/ARE NOT TO BE COLLECTED AND STORED
/ANALOG KNOB 0 ALLOWS ONE TO MOVE THE AVERAGE UP AND DOWN ON THE SCOPE.
/STARTING ADDRESS OF THE PROGRAM IS
/           00300 IN LINC
/AND IS STORED UNDER DATACOL.
/ALL ENTRIES ARE IN OCTAL - THIS IS NOT
/CHECKED. MINIMUM BIN TIME IS ONE MSEC
/     SYNC PULSE GOES INTO INPUT 1
/     DATA IS SAMPLED AT A/D CHANNEL 10
/     SPIKES GO TO INPUT 3
/IF N SAMPLES ARE TAKEN AND ARE TO BE
/AVERAGED, THE N SAMPLES
/ARE WRITTEN TO TAPE IN CONSECUTIVE
/BLOCKS. BLOCK N+1 RECEIVES THE AVERAGE
/BLOCK N+2 RECEIVES THE SPIKE POST STIMULUS HIST.
/THE PROGRAM SKIPS TAPE BLOCKS 270 THRU
/467 AS THAT IS THE ASSEMBLERS AREA OF TAPE WITH ITS INDEX.
/THIS PROGRAM HANDLES ONLY 256 BINS (400 OCTAL)
/THIS CONTINUES SUCCESIVELY UNTIL THE
/TAPE IS FULL OR THE COMPUTER IS STOPPED
/WHEN THE TAPE IS FULL, A "T" IS TYPED
/AND THE BELL RINGS. CHANGE TAPE AND 
/DEPRESS SN0. THE BLOCK NUMBER BEING WRITTEN IS 
/DISPLAYED IN THE UPPER LEFT OF THE SCOPE
/
/
/NOTE TO NATICK
/INDEX REGISTER "AVGPTR" AND TAPE BLOCK
/WORD POINTER "WRTBLK" SHOULD BE DECREMENTED IF YOU
/WISH TO DELETE A PARTICULAR INDIVIDUAL WAVEFORM
/I HAVENT DETERMINED HOW TO SUBTRACT THAT WAVEFORM FROM THE AVERAGE THO.
